From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:56:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] layout: vertex markers

marker-start, marker-mid and marker-end, placed per SVG 2: outgoing
direction at the first vertex, incoming at the last, the bisector of the
two at interior corners, with a closed subpath folding its closing edge
into the first vertex so a polygon's corners bisect properly.
auto-start-reverse flips only the start marker, markerUnits=strokeWidth
scales by the resolved stroke width, refX/refY are mapped through the
marker's own viewBox before aligning with the vertex, and content clips
to the marker viewport -- expressed in content coordinates as the
viewport rectangle pulled back through the viewBox mapping, so the
existing group clip does the work.

The placement math is pure and lives in svg/marker.rs with eight tests;
the marker definitions ride the same one-pass id scan as gradients and
clip paths; and marker content is walked like <use> content, at
use-depth plus one, so a circular marker reference cannot hang layout.

Markers render even when the shape itself paints nothing, which the
spec requires and which also meant moving the shape-visibility early
return below the marker check.

The three properties are gecko-gated in stylo -- the fifth instance of
that trap, after pointer-events, stop-color/stop-opacity and
text-anchor/dominant-baseline -- so this needs stylo-0005, and the
attributes are mapped as presentational hints like the rest.

One knowing imprecision, recorded in the module: paths containing arcs
were flattened to cubics at construction, so each arc contributes
phantom interior vertices and marker-mid fires on them. Fixing it means
carrying vertex provenance through the flattening.

Validated: double-ended arrows with auto-start-reverse, dots on every
polyline vertex, an arrowhead rotated to a curve's end tangent, and
markers on an invisible path all match the rasterization path to 0.066%
of pixels. Mermaid diagrams now have their arrowheads, completing the
picture: themed, labelled, edged, and pointed. svg/ WPT +369 against
the pref-off baseline, up from +360, same six known regressions.
